ngs suggest a more immediate concern", "Bowel obstruction: considered given the abdominal distension and tympanitic abdomen, but the severe hypertension and cardiac findings suggest a more systemic issue"], "alarm_features": ["Severe hypertension (197/128 mmHg)", "Tachycardia (100/min)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Acute Gastrointestinal Distress with Severe Hypertension", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.06907069267804068, "posterior": 0.07217042383838448, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Severe hypertension and tachycardia provide weak support for Acute Gastrointestinal Distress with Severe Hypertension."], "evidence_against": ["The absence of specific gastrointestinal symptoms weakly argues against Acute Gastrointestinal Distress with Severe Hypertension."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Cardiovascular Complication with Gastrointestinal Symptoms", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.19714461910942402, "posterior": 0.21958170728627902, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The systolic murmur provides weak support for Cardiovascular Complication with Gastrointestinal Symptoms."], "evidence_against": ["The absence of typical cardiovascular symptoms weakly argues against Cardiovascular Complication with Gastrointestinal Symptoms."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3", "B2.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representat